  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, I was thinking a bit and it suddenly occurred to me that the solution for the unity version problem is actually pretty simple. \nA limbo loader world. \n\nThe user logs into vrchat and is placed in a universal home room with dx12/vulkan and dx11 build target capabilities. The new menu shows a split with 201x worlds and 5.6.3p legacy worlds and avatars. \n\nA warning will pop up if you're using an avatar that isn't supported in the 201x only worlds before you go, and at that time the client switches versions or launches another instance while sleeping the loader. When you exit, you bounce back and forth between builds using the universal loading world as an in between \"limbo\" which it seems you already have the framework for with the \"Go\" button. It could be pretty transparent. You could set an avatar for legacy and new worlds. This would bridge the gap for all players and allow you to retain old content until players migrate. \n\nAlso, teaching people to add build targets in unity would go a long way, since if dx12/vulkan is included, the world will upgrade to the new engine without too much lighting and shader trouble cross framework.",
